  <prompt>Implement the H10 Dataverse Application User + Graph app-role parity handler as an IJobHandler in the L2 control-plane. H10 registers 2 App Users (BFF app-reg + UAMI) as System Administrator on the target Dataverse env, then syncs Graph app-role parity from Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs constant onto the UAMI service principal. Interim uses PPAC UI + Graph SDK (design target TF powerplatform_user deferred per M-10). H10 escalation gate: 10 of 14 null AppRoleId GUIDs in GraphAppRoles.cs MUST be completed BEFORE first production customer. Idempotency key: appuser-{customerId}.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IJobHandler contract, Microsoft Graph SDK v6 / Kiota 2.0 (ODataError), Dataverse Application User registration via Web API systemusers upsert, GraphAppRoles.cs 14-role compile-time constant (r3 task 062), T2 + T3 silent-fail trap verification. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.cs exists, implements IJobHandler, registers in L2 DI, and: (a) registers BFF app-reg AND UAMI as System Administrator App Users on target Dataverse env; (b) reads all 14 role IDs from GraphAppRoles.cs constant and grants them onto UAMI SP via Graph API; (c) verifies T2: `systemusers?$filter=applicationid eq {uami-app-id}` returns count 1; (d) verifies T3: UAMI SP appRoleAssignments includes ALL 14 role IDs from GraphAppRoles.cs (fails deploy with trap-T3 code otherwise); (e) H10 escalation: if any AppRoleId in GraphAppRoles.cs is null (indicating Phase A GUID completion incomplete), fail deploy with distinct escalation code BEFORE granting; (f) asserts idempotency key appuser-{customerId}. Unit tests cover happy path, T2 verify fail, T3 verify fail (partial roles), H10 escalation on null GUID, and idempotency.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-13 + FR-33 (T2 + T3) + design.md §4.1 H10 + §4B T2/T3: H10 owns two silent-fail traps. T2 = MI not registered as Dataverse App User (leads to fleet-wide 403 on Dataverse calls). T3 = UAMI Graph app-role parity broken (leads to silent 403 on app-only Graph calls). GraphAppRoles.cs r3 task 062 is the compile-time constant for 14 roles; 10 of 14 GUIDs are null pending Phase A az-enumeration completion. TF migration deferred per M-10.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs (r3 task 062 constant)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Grant-GraphAppRoles.ps1 (Phase B — task 015)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="036" status="pending">L2 project scaffold — Wave C3</dependency>
      <dependency task="049" status="pending">H6 solution import — solutions must exist before App User registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">Phase B Grant-GraphAppRoles.ps1 script</dependency>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">Phase A GraphAppRoles.cs GUID completion (10 of 14 null AppRoleIds via `az` enumeration)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Single IJobHandler implementation registered in L2 DI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register in L2 control-plane, NOT BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth ceremony 21 MUSTs; Dataverse App User registration for both BFF app-reg + UAMI + Graph parity are specific MUSTs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Reuse background-job infrastructure; return 202; fire-and-forget.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">systemuserid + applicationid + role IDs written to Cosmos follow GUID canonicalization (lowercase, no braces).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key: appuser-{customerId} — App User registration is per-customer + version-independent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">H10 owns T2 (spec.md FR-33): `systemusers?$filter=applicationid eq {uami-app-id}` returns count 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">H10 owns T3 (spec.md FR-33): UAMI SP `appRoleAssignments` includes ALL 14 role IDs from GraphAppRoles.cs; fails deploy with trap-T3 code on any missing role.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">H10 escalation gate (spec.md MUST rule): if any AppRoleId GUID in GraphAppRoles.cs is null (Phase A incomplete), fail deploy with "H10EscalationGate" BEFORE granting; do NOT grant with null GUIDs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Interim implementation uses PPAC UI + Graph SDK per M-10; TF migration is NOT r1 acceptance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I1">-TenantId flows explicitly to all Graph + Dataverse calls; no default tenant fallback.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I5">Graph token acquisition per-tenant scoped: app-only calls use .default scope with target tenant's tid explicitly; NOT MI credential default tenant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md NFR-09">Graph SDK calls catch ODataError (not ServiceException); ResponseStatusCode is int; ResponseHeaders is dict.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>L2 handler for Dataverse App User + Graph app-role parity with T2 + T3 trap ownership</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
