    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="reference-handler-shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/">IJobHandler exemplar.</pattern>
      <pattern name="dataverse-token-cache" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs">Cross-env token cache pattern.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (FULL) and load knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Author H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.cs — inject IDataverseWebApiClient, IGraphAppOnlyClient, IPowerShellRunner, IIdempotencyService, ICosmosRunStore, plus IGraphAppRolesRegistry (reads GraphAppRoles.cs constant).</step>
    <step order="2">H10 escalation gate: iterate GraphAppRoles.cs entries; if any AppRoleId is null (default Guid.Empty), fail deploy with "H10EscalationGate" BEFORE any Graph or Dataverse write.</step>
    <step order="3">Register BFF app-reg AND UAMI as Dataverse System Administrator App Users via Dataverse Web API systemusers upsert on target env.</step>
    <step order="4">Grant all 14 roles from GraphAppRoles.cs onto UAMI SP via Graph API; wrap Graph SDK calls in try/catch ODataError (NFR-09).</step>
    <step order="5">Verify T2: query `systemusers?$filter=applicationid eq {uami-app-id}`; fail with trap-T2 code if count != 1.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify T3: query UAMI SP appRoleAssignments; assert ALL 14 role IDs from GraphAppRoles.cs are present; fail with trap-T3 code on any missing role (name the missing roles in diagnostic).</step>
    <step order="7">Write systemUserId (UAMI + BFF app-reg) to Cosmos interStepState.</step>
    <step order="8">Author unit tests: (a) happy path — T2 + T3 both verified, (b) T2 verify fail — App User not registered, (c) T3 verify fail — 13 of 14 roles present, (d) H10 escalation — GraphAppRoles.cs has null AppRoleId, (e) idempotency.</step>
    <step order="9">Register in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="10">Run dotnet build + dotnet test; verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change task 053 status from 🔲 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviations in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If Graph app-role sync returns PARTIAL roles (T3 fails despite `az` enumeration completing — indicates one or more GUID values in GraphAppRoles.cs are WRONG, not just null), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT retry; operator must diagnose which GUID is incorrect via `az ad sp show --id 00000003-0000-0000-c000-000000000000` role enumeration.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Phase A GraphAppRoles.cs GUID completion (task 005) is not merged, DEFER this task — do NOT run H10 with null AppRoleIds under any circumstances (H10 escalation gate is BINDING).</trigger>
    <trigger>If T2 verification fails but Dataverse Web API systemusers upsert returned 200 (silent Dataverse write success + query miss), STOP and escalate — could indicate Dataverse env is not fully replicated post-H5.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs (r3 task 062 constant — 14-role compile-time list). No existing L2 handler for Dataverse App User + Graph parity.</existing>
    <extension>No — H10 needs to own T2 + T3 trap post-conditions and the H10 escalation gate (null-GUID check). PS script alone can't provide DAG advancement + trap verification + escalation-gate branching.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H10 owning T2 + T3, MI-Dataverse-App-User missing = fleet-wide 403 on every BFF → Dataverse call (T2 silent fail per §4B). UAMI Graph app-role parity broken = app-only Graph calls silently 403 (T3 silent fail per §4B). Both are CATASTROPHIC in production and were the exact traps §4B catalog was created to enforce.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">az CLI for role enumeration</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.Tests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given all 14 AppRoleId GUIDs in GraphAppRoles.cs are populated (Phase A complete), when HandleAsync runs, then BFF app-reg + UAMI are both registered as System Administrator App Users on target Dataverse env AND all 14 Graph app-roles are granted onto UAMI SP.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T2 (spec.md FR-33): `systemusers?$filter=applicationid eq {uami-app-id}` returns count 1; H10 fails with trap-T2 code if not.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T3 (spec.md FR-33): UAMI SP appRoleAssignments includes all 14 role IDs from GraphAppRoles.cs; H10 fails with trap-T3 code + diagnostic naming missing roles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H10 escalation (spec.md MUST rule): given any AppRoleId in GraphAppRoles.cs is null (default Guid.Empty), when HandleAsync runs, then it fails with "H10EscalationGate" BEFORE any Graph or Dataverse write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: two invocations for the same customerId — second call is a no-op (appuser-{customerId} match); systemusers upsert alt-key + Graph role grant idempotent per role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: H10 invoked without tenantId parameter returns failure (§4D I1 + I5); Graph tokens acquired with explicit tenantId, not MI default tenant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graph SDK calls catch ODataError (NFR-09 Kiota 2.0).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; dotnet build + dotnet test exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-13 + FR-33 (T2 + T3) + MUST rules + NFR-09; design.md §4.1 H10 + §4B T2/T3 + M-10 TF deferral. Phase A completion of 10 of 14 null GUIDs is a BINDING escalation gate BEFORE first production customer provisioning.</notes>

  <execution>
